# Architecture Rules

- Use Next.js App Router and TypeScript.
- Keep source adapter logic inside `lib/sources`.
- Keep provider-agnostic AI provider and prompt logic inside `lib/ai`.
- Keep orchestration inside `lib/pipeline`.
- Keep MVP storage inside `lib/storage` using mock/in-memory storage.
- Do not add PostgreSQL or Prisma in the MVP.
- Prepare persistence-ready types so database storage can be added later.
- Use DeepSeek V4 Pro as the default AI config (`provider: deepseek`, `model: deepseek-v4-pro`) through `AI_PROVIDER`, `AI_MODEL`, and `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`.
- Do not hardcode DeepSeek throughout the architecture; use an AI provider abstraction.
- Do not call external APIs directly from React components.
- Do not call AI provider SDKs directly from React components.
- All API inputs must be validated with Zod.
- All AI outputs must be validated with Zod.
- Prefer small composable functions over large files.
- Do not introduce new libraries unless they solve a clear problem.
- Build mock pipeline before real external API integrations.
- Keep code typed, explicit, and easy to extend.
